/*
 * Zephyr's rpi_5 takes zephyr,sram from the SoC's sram0
 * (dts/arm64/broadcom/bcm2712.dtsi: 512 KiB at 0x200000, two address cells).
 * The deqp image carries the V3D's 48 MiB carve-out, 16 MiB of tiled texture
 * copies, the compiler's 8 MiB scratch, its keep region and the 64 MiB C heap
 * as statics, so it gets 256 MiB from 0x200000, the size of the Pi 4's deqp
 * window (boards/rpi_4b.overlay) at the Pi 5's load address. The firmware
 * loads a kernel= image at 0x200000 and puts the DTB at 0x2efec600
 * (driver/docs/rpi5-v3d71-facts.md, U6), above the image's end (0x10200000),
 * and the range stays below 4 GiB, so the V3D's page table entries and the
 * mailbox's buffer address fit (pre-study-rpi5.md, U10). Zephyr's own
 * mailbox driver (mbox0) stays disabled, as bcm2712.dtsi has it: the board
 * layer's rpi_mbox.c owns the mailbox.
 */
&sram0 {
	reg = <0x0 0x200000 0x10000000>;
};
